<title>NETHERLANDS: Labouchere raises HBG to a Buy.</title>
<headline>Labouchere raises HBG to a Buy.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of January research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>HBG		 construction  375.00  Bank Labouchere</p>
<p>COMMENT: Buy (from Hold).</p>
<p>Company announced takeovers of Britain's Higgs &amp; Hill and Germany's Ways &amp; Freytag in December. Although both firms are expected to suffer a loss in 1996, we consider acquisitions reasonably priced. HBG shares by all means cheap. Prospective PE is among lowest in the sector and represent a 34 percent discount to the AEX-index. 12-month target is 450 guilders.</p>
<p>    Estimates (Dfl):   EPS	  P/E     Dividend</p>
<p>    1995 (actual)	29.91	8.2     12.80</p>
<p>    1996		   35.79     10.5     13.36</p>
<p>    1997		   38.28	9.8     15.33</p>
<p>    1998		   43.03	8.7     17.21</p>
